# Evening MCQ — 15 class + 5 real PYQ

Ghost Recall stays **8 Q / 60 min** in the morning. Do not mix the two formats.

## Hard limits

- **20 items, one message:** **15** from Nik’s notes + **5 authentic UPSC CSE Prelims PYQs**.
- Answer in one reply (`1-b, 2-a, …`; `pass` allowed). Do **not** run sequential Q&A.
- Scoring: **+2 / −0.66**. Max **40**. Unattempted = 0.
- Target **~45 min**. If it overruns, keep 20 but shorten stems — do not bleed into Ghost Recall.

## Mix

| Count | Source |
|:---:|:---|
| ~8 | Today’s class(es) |
| 2–3 | Due Mistake Bank traps |
| rest of 15 | Older notes (not tomorrow’s Ghost Recall dump) |
| **5** | Real PYQs only — topics he **already has notes** for. Cite **year** (and Q no. if known). Label them **PYQ**. Never invent a “PYQ.” |

## PYQ extra info → enrichment, not a new topic

Same rule as newspaper already-covered: append `### Update — D Month YYYY (UPSC CSE Prelims YYYY)` on the **original** note. New facts only. Patch that cluster’s knowledge graph. **Do not** add a Day-1 Ghost Recall row.
